{title: 166 - Christ the Lord Is Risen Today}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #166 • WORGAN  (WITH  ALLELUJAS) • 11.10.9.12}
{lyricist: Charles Wesley}
{composer: Lyra Davidica}
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 166}
{meta: tune WORGAN  (WITH  ALLELUJAS)}
{meta: meter 11.10.9.12}
{meta: category Jesus Christ - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[C]Christ the Lord [F/A]is risen [C]today, [Am]Al leluia!
[F/A]Sons [C]of [Em]men [C]and [G]angels [C/E]say, [Dm]Al [Am]leluia!
[G]Raise [Am]your [G7/F]joys [C/E]and triumphs [G]high, Al leluia!
[G/D]Sing, ye heavens, [C]and [F]earth [C]reply, Allelu [G7]ia!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[C]Lives again [F/C]our [C]glorious King, [Am]Alleluia!
[F/A]Where, [C]O [Em]death, [C]is [G]now [C]thy sting? [Dm]Alleluia!
[G]Once [Am]he [G/B]died [C/E]our [Dm]souls [G]to save, Alleluia!
[G/D]Where's thy [G7/F]victory, [C]boasting grave? [Dm]Alleluia!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[C]Love's redeeming work is done, [Am]Alleluia!
[F/A]Fought [C]the [Em]fight, [C]the [G]battle [C/E]won, [Dm]Alleluia!
[G]Death [Am]in [G/B]vain [C/E]forbids [G]him rise, Alleluia!
[G/D]Christ has opened [F/A]paradise, [C]Alleluia!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[C]Soar we now [F]where [C]Christ has led, [Dm]Alleluia!
[F/A]Following [Dm]our [C/G]exalted Head, [Am]Alleluia!
[G]Made [Am]like [G/B]him, [C/E]like [Dm]him [G]we rise, Alleluia!
[G/D]Ours the cross, [C/E]the [F/A]grave, [C]the skies, Alleluia!
{end_of_verse}
